<title>MEXICO: RESEARCH ALERT-Hylsamex downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Hylsamex downgraded.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Banamex-Accival brokerage has lowered its recommendation for steelmaker Hylsamex to reduce from neutral.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Arturo Espinosa said in a research report dated July 18 the recommendation had changed due to a sharp rise in the share price.</p>
<p>-- &quot;We no longer see the stock as undervalued when looking at Hylsamex's contribution to cash flow for (it's holding company) Alfa,&quot; Espinosa wrote.</p>
<p>-- Espinosa noted Hylsamex, for the year to date, had outperformed other Mexican steelmakers Ahmsa and Tamsa.</p>
<p>Hylsamex B shares were down 80 centavos to 51.70 pesos in late trade on the Mexican bourse on Monday. Alfa A shares had meanwhile declined 40 centavos to 56.10 pesos.</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7907))</p>
